Stack: Vite + React 18 + TypeScript + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui + React Router v6 + TanStack Query v5
Backend: Go API at the URL in VITE_API_URL env var, JWT in Authorization: Bearer <token> header
Response format from backend: { "data": ..., "error": ... }

## Architecture
- src/api/ — API client functions, one file per resource (auth.ts, watchlist.ts, tmdb.ts)
- src/components/ — reusable UI components
- src/components/ui/ — shadcn primitives (don't manually edit, regenerate via CLI)
- src/hooks/ — custom React hooks
- src/lib/ — utilities, helpers
- src/pages/ — page-level components, one per route
- src/providers/ — React Context providers (auth, etc.)
- src/types/ — TypeScript type definitions

## Code Organization
- When ADDING new functions/hooks to an EXISTING file, append at the bottom unless tightly coupled to an existing function (then place immediately after).
- When CREATING a new file, organize logically (exports first, then helpers, then types if inline).
- One default export per page/component file. Named exports for utilities.

## Data Provenance Comments
When data is passed through 2+ component layers, or comes from a hook whose origin isn't obvious at the call site, add a comment at the destination:
  // src: <component or hook> via <intermediate layers if relevant>
Examples:
  // src: useWatchlistQuery (TanStack Query, fetches GET /watchlist)
  // src: AuthContext.user via App > Layout > Header
  // src: parent SearchPage, passed as 'result' prop
Skip for data defined in the same file or obviously one layer up.

## TypeScript
- Strict mode (no implicit any, no implicit returns).
- Define types for every API request/response in src/types/api.ts.
- Prefer `type` for unions and primitives, `interface` for object shapes.
- Never use `any` without a // TODO: type this properly comment.

## API Client
- All backend calls go through src/api/ functions.
- Components NEVER call fetch directly — they call hooks (which call API functions).
- Centralize JWT attachment in src/api/client.ts (the fetch wrapper).
- On 401 response, clear localStorage auth_token and redirect to /login.

## Auth
- JWT stored in localStorage under key "auth_token".
- AuthProvider exposes: user, isAuthenticated, login(), logout(), register().
- Protected routes wrap with a <RequireAuth> component that redirects to /login.

## State
- Server state (data from backend): TanStack Query useQuery/useMutation, NEVER useState.
- Client state (modal open, form input): useState or Context.
- Never duplicate server state in client state — read directly from useQuery.

## Styling
- Tailwind utility classes only. No external CSS files except index.css for base.
- Use shadcn/ui components for primitives. Don't write custom Button/Input/Dialog from scratch.
- Use cn() from lib/utils.ts for conditional class merging.

## What NOT to do
- Never call fetch directly from a component.
- Never put JWT in URL params or component props.
- Never store passwords on the FE.
- Never use Redux, MobX, Zustand, Recoil — Context + useState is enough.
- Never use class components — function components and hooks only.
- Never introduce a new dependency without confirming with the developer first.
- Never expose backend error messages directly to UI — wrap them in user-friendly messages.

## Delivery
- Show all diffs before applying.
- For new files, briefly explain what they do.
- Match existing file patterns when adding to them.
- If you create a new pattern, explicitly note it and explain why.
